      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The board should absolutely pivot towards 'equality of outcome' metrics in our credit scoring logic. This is not just a moral imperative but a strategic one. By focusing on outcomes, we can directly address systemic inequalities that have long been ignored. Traditional 'equality of opportunity' metrics are fundamentally flawed because they assume a level playing field, which we know doesn't exist. Our firm has a responsibility to lead by example and ensure that our financial practices contribute to a more equitable society. This shift will not only enhance our reputation but also attract a more diverse customer base and foster long-term sustainability. Traditionalists may resist, but the evidence and moral case for this change are overwhelming.",
      "source": "target",
